## 4. What these examples establish

Supported:

\[
\boxed{
\text{organization at one level}
\rightarrow
\text{collective mode / constraint}
\rightarrow
\text{new effective interaction}
\rightarrow
\text{new collective organization}
}
\]

This mechanism occurs in more than one distinct physical system.

Therefore RRG does **not** need to invent the possibility that lower-level organization can create a higher-level effective interaction.

---

## 5. What remains open

These examples do **not** prove:

\[
\boxed{
\text{strong, weak, EM, gravity}
=
\text{four successive RRG resonant levels}
}
\]

They also do not prove that all forces are literally scalar frequencies.

The locked core remains unchanged.

The stronger RRG extension remains:

\[
\boxed{
R_n=(G_n,M_n)
\rightarrow
\mathcal I_{n+1}^{\rm eff}
\rightarrow
R_{n+1}
}
\]

where \(\mathcal I^{\rm eff}\) is an effective interaction channel generated, activated, or made dominant by the organization at level \(n\).

The next research question is:

> **Under what general conditions does a resonant geometry generate an effective interaction channel that stabilizes or enables a new higher-level resonant geometry?**
